\paragraph{Position mediation.} Position ($t/T$) accounts for 9--20pp of balanced accuracy,\footnote{R1-32B's 20.4pp drop reflects $W{=}1$; at $W{\geq}3$, drops are 9--17pp.} but all models retain non-positional signal above chance (all $p{<}0.001$; \cref{app:position_residual}). Three of four models retain significant non-positional HS advantage (residualized gap +3.7 to +6.9pp, HB corrected); R1-32B's gap is +1.9pp ($p{=}0.914$, $n{=}20$), well below the MDE of ${\sim}$9pp and thus indistinguishable from zero at current power. Quadratic residualization (adding $(t/T)^2$) is computed for all four models: 2/4 retain significance (R1-8B +10.3pp, OT-7B +9.8pp, both HB), while R1-32B (0.0pp) and QwQ-32B ($-$1.0pp) do not (\cref{tab:position_quadratic}). QwQ-32B's HS advantage is fully absorbed by the quadratic position term, meaning the information captured by the probe overlaps substantially with non-linear position. Temporal windowing reduces position dependence (\cref{sec:temporal}).\looseness=-1

\paragraph{Caveats.} Nested 5-fold CV confirms the HS precision advantage at 7--8B (10/10 folds, 13--25\% shrinkage; \cref{app:nested_cv}); the +21.9pp OT-7B holdout estimate is an upper bound (nested CV selects L21--27 vs.\ holdout L16). R1-32B achieves significance only at $W{=}1$ (25\% coverage); QwQ-32B lead time is negative ($-$1.2 to +1.9 steps). FPR remains 11--50\%, so current methods characterize the phenomenon rather than constitute production detectors.\looseness=-1

\subsection{32B Model-Specific Analysis}\label{sec:32b-analysis}

Results are exploratory ($n{=}19$--$20$; MDE at 80\% power: 8.6--9.5pp, \cref{app:power_analysis}; effects below MDE marked * in \cref{tab:32b_divergence}). Both 32B models lack nested CV; LOO-CV and multi-seed analyses (\cref{app:layer_sweep,app:multi_seed}) provide partial robustness checks. R1-32B and QwQ-32B share the Qwen-32B architecture but present opposite detection profiles (\cref{tab:32b_divergence}); replication with $n{\geq}50$ traces is needed.\looseness=-1

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\resizebox{\columnwidth}{!}{%
\begin{tabular}{lcccc}
\toprule
\textbf{Model} & \textbf{Cov.} & \textbf{Lead (steps)} & \textbf{HB} & \textbf{Pos.\ margin} \\
\midrule
R1-32B$^\dagger$ & 25\% & +11.7 to +13.3 & \checkmark{} ($W{=}1$) & +14.2pp \\
QwQ-32B$^\dagger$ & 74\% & $-$1.2 to +1.9 & \checkmark{} (all $W$) & $-$3.6pp* \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}}
\caption{32B cross-model divergence ($\dagger$\,$n \leq 20$, all exploratory; MDE 8.6--9.5pp). HB: passes Holm-Bonferroni ($\alpha{=}0.05$). Pos.\ margin: HS BA$-$position baseline. *\,Below MDE.}
\label{tab:32b_divergence}
\end{table}

R1-32B suggests commitment 11--13 steps early (+14.2pp over position) but covers only 25\% of traces ($W{=}1$); its precision effect (+15.4pp) falls below MDE. QwQ-32B achieves significance at all window sizes (74\% coverage) but with negative lead time; the position baseline achieves higher BA (0.832 vs.\ 0.796, margin +4.5pp, $p{=}0.133$, NS at $n{=}19$; \cref{app:position_residual}). Per-model validation is needed.\looseness=-1

\subsection{Temporal Context}\label{sec:temporal}

Temporal windowing ($W{>}1$) improves both modalities (\cref{fig:window_ablation}): at 7--8B, the modality advantage (+20.1 to +21.9pp) exceeds temporal improvement (+13pp). GRU models achieve comparable accuracy but higher FPR (\cref{tab:gru_multi_seeds,app:temporal_details}); an adaptive two-stage strategy offers marginal gains (\cref{app:two_stage}). CP-aligned probe trajectories confirm sharper HS transitions at the commitment point (\cref{fig:trajectory}); precision gaps across encoder conditions appear in \cref{fig:forest_precision}.\looseness=-1

\subsection{Negative Results}\label{sec:negative}

No alternative method consistently matches supervised probing (\cref{tab:negative}). BOCPD~\citep{adams2007bayesian}/CUSUM fail (0\% detection on 3/4 models); Mahalanobis yields near-zero separation; RepE~\citep{zou2023representation} is model-dependent (BA 0.756 vs.\ 0.559); MLP probes overfit; CCS misaligns temporally; cross-model transfer fails (\cref{app:negative_details}). The signal is directional, gradual, model-specific, and linearly separable, which excludes change-point, distance, transfer, and objective-alignment methods respectively.\looseness=-1

